  <figcaption>
    <strong id="flow-title">
      Message content is encrypted at the endpoints.
    </strong>{" "}
    <span id="flow-desc">
      Clients exchange MLS ciphertext through NATS and JetStream. A separate
      metadata backend manages public identities and authorization without chat
      keys. An explicitly invited service participant occupies the same
      plaintext boundary as a client endpoint. Files are encrypted in Object
      Store; their keys and metadata travel inside MLS. Receipts use a separate
      encrypted, non-durable Core NATS path. The broker sees routing and traffic
      metadata. This full message path runs in the static development fixture
      without TLS; dynamic messaging integration is still in progress.
    </span>
  </figcaption>
